**corollary 22.4 (GPC4).** For every i<j there are primes p|B_i and q|B_j with both h_p,h_q odd and (q/p)=-1. For every fixed i, at least one such p has infinitely many distinct later witnesses q. In particular there are infinitely many split primes q with odd h_q, (q/19)=-1, and rho(q)=pi(q)=2*3^s for some s>=3.

